{"title":"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ordered_pair\" title=\"Ordered pair\">ordered pairs</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c628adf51cbdfde8f78a3615b70961cdcea931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x \\le 1, 0&lt;y\\le 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d3cb912be801f55cdbf561e733be8ec8307ed92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\log_2{\\left(\\frac 1x\\right)}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"97\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/6976ef44fa275593ec211e21c8b9948741127a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\log_5{\\left(\\frac 1y\\right)}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"96\" height=\"45\" /> are both even. Given that the area of the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> The notation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1f0e0581826ae7502d664a79329503eb58c073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor{z}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Floor_function\" title=\"Floor function\">greatest integer</a> that is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c0a7013ecf089e9a9e98f59b01428e7fee4be86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c914610513932b3418db54c690b40b15584bee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\log_2\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"91\" height=\"43\" /> is even when\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/613a80c45b75bd2e3a1a3d0b6808c97a8ae41536.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\in \\left(\\frac{1}{2},1\\right] \\cup \\left(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{1}{4}\\right] \\cup \\left(\\frac{1}{32},\\frac{1}{16}\\right] \\cup \\cdots\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Likewise:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a52a459eec4a15b933df0bb6ffd9e4e123cfa4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\log_5\\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"90\" height=\"43\" /> is even when\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314ecb43636fa7e10ee4ef14f6c751dcbf4ff4f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y \\in \\left(\\frac{1}{5},1\\right] \\cup \\left(\\frac{1}{125},\\frac{1}{25}\\right] \\cup \\left(\\frac{1}{3125},\\frac{1}{625}\\right] \\cup \\cdots\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Graphing this yields a series of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangles</a> which become smaller as you move toward the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Origin\" title=\"Origin\">origin</a>. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> interval of each box is given by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">geometric sequence</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/889dbec7e90e800ded0a61b94f246c8e683009e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} , \\frac{1}{8}, \\frac{1}{32}, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" />, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> interval is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/3617d7b815fbd80e9aa3152a4b6f77b74ccbc564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} , \\frac{4}{125}, \\frac{4}{3125}, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Each box is the product of one term of each sequence. The sum of these boxes is simply the product of the sum of each sequence or:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/63087ddd18ec20f71058f90f4746b0b2993fc34f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{32} \\ldots \\right)\\left(\\frac{4}{5} + \\frac{4}{125} + \\frac{4}{3125} \\ldots \\right)=\\left(\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{4}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\frac{4}{5}}{1-\\frac{1}{25}}\\right)= \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{5}{9},\\]\" width=\"597\" height=\"46\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8efb9250ac268b5b9afd015dd79ef976ceebc2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = 5 + 9 = \\boxed{014}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I\" title=\"2004 AIME I\">2004 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202818\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 190/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4634/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.918      1 -total\n 58.14%    7.511      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.85%    5.019      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2677:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202818 and revision id 273519. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}